codex
Program fidelity is exact at the translator boundary, and the candidate matches the canonical implementation throughout the non-empty integer domain sampled, including both decision boundaries and negative integers. I also found a real scope limitation: if “numbers” were interpreted to include non-integral floats, the two Python implementations can diverge; the K model admits only integer list elements. I’ll keep that separate from proof soundness while I rebuild both definitions from source.
